WEBVTT

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.680
He's gotten better.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.060
Otoya's bright aura already draws people in,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.680
but it's been getting even brighter.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.890
There may be some secret behind it.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.230
Now that you mention it...

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.240
Did you know that he disappears sometimes?

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.660
Maybe he's been doing voice training.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.330
Without telling us?

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.160
Really? Ikki is?

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.710
We have to keep up.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.350
What?

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.720
You were all listening?

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.890
Otoya.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.810
Huh? What?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.480
If you don't hurry, you'll be late to your recording.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.940
Oh, no!

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.190
I'm going to appear on this show?

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.030
Cecil and I are going on together?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.110
Why me?

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.530
Shut up and follow orders.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.740
I don't know what Saotome is thinking,

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.210
putting an amateur like you on a variety show...

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.830
Cecil!

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.340
Let's make it a blast!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.670
It'll be okay.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.550
Just do what you want, like you did during the karuta match.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.840
Try to have fun.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.550
Have fun?

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.430
Our next guests are these two members of the Shining Agency!

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.140
Come on out!

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:37.070
Yeah! I'm Ittoki Otoya from ST☆RISH.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.650
I'm Aijima Cecil from Agnapolis.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.910
Let's jump right in and have Aijima Cecil do some impressions for us.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.660
What? Impressions?

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.080
Hold on. Cecil still doesn't know that much about Japan,

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.000
so he's not familiar with famous people...

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.620
Impressions...

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.630
Of animals, or anything else you want.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.210
Famous people...

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.750
Otoya, it's okay.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:00.420
Huh?

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.380
Here I go.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:07.510
Do you know who I am?

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.890
Could it be...

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.140
Shining Saotome!

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:14.850
Bingo, bingo, bingo!

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:19.020
You all seem to be very sharp.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.940
Mister Ittoki.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:21.990
Y-Yes?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.700
Work good and hard.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.280
O-Okay!

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.700
<i>Why did he have to do an impression of him?</i>

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.410
<i>It's pretty good too.</i>

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:40.630
Okay, President. Tell me how I can become big like you.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.840
Oh, that's impossible.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.380
You won't grow any more at your age.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.010
You mean my height?

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.600
I'm asking how I can become big as an idol!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.770
Oh, Japanese is so complicated.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.560
You're complicated, Cecil!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.320
Okay, let's move on!

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:04.360
Today, we'll be entertaining you until the very end!

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.280
Cecil!

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.660
That was so much fun.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.830
That was amazing, Cecil.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.620
I've never been to such a fun recording before.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.340
Was that all right?

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.630
Everyone was laughing a lot.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.960
What are you talking about?

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.930
It was great, Cecil.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.890
Because you have been receiving instruction directly from me,

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.510
it's only natural you were successful.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.720
What?

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.520
Oh, there you are.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:39.060
Cecil, the director wants to talk to you.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.320
Yes, we will go speak to him immediately.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.980
Let's go, Aijima.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.360
Oh, okay.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:53.200
Um, good work today.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.080
What? No, thank you.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.960
Good work today.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:58.870
See you later.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.920
What a weird guy.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.180
There's a featured article about Hijirikawa's play.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.060
There's one for Shou's <i>Prince of Fighting</i> show too.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:25.980
This is amazing. I'll show everyone when they get home.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.360
Huh? Where am I?

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.870
Am I lost?

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.950
What am I going to do?

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.160
Otobro, you're slow!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.120
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:40.120
Hurry up! Over here!

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.920
Don't pull so much.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.460
Ittoki?

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.800
Otobro, look at this!

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.970
Let me see.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.930
Wow, that's amazing.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.640
Isn't it awesome?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.140
What is he doing here?

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.520
It's a suspicious person!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.430
What?

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.180
A suspicious person!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.270
Nanami?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:13.030
Principal, um, this is...

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.950
I'm Nanami Haruka. I'm sorry about what happened earlier.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:22.210
Oh, so you're... I've heard so much about you from Otoya.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:22.750
What?

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.710
I'm so pleased to meet you.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.670
Y-You surprised me. What are you doing here, Nanami?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.510
I went to do some shopping on the way home from my meeting, but...

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.850
Were you lost again?

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:37.890
Yes.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.310
You haven't changed.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.270
Otoya, I'm sorry. There's something I need to do.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.810
Nanami, take your time.

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:48.110
Okay.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.660
I grew up here.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.820
What?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:02.620
My mom died when I was little, and I don't know who my dad is.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.370
That's awful...

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.750
Sorry, I must have shocked you by springing this on you.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.760
But it's not a depressing story at all.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.930
Anyway, I'm sure people would worry about me if they knew.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.010
That's why I haven't told anyone.

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.310
Ittoki...

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.390
I love this place.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:27.020
That's why I still stop by from time to time even after I left.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:33.070
This place is my home.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.950
Your home...

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:36.820
Oh, I know!

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.330
They're going to open a bazaar here soon.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.370
The children look forward to it every year.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.040
Why don't you come, Nanami?

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.830
A bazaar?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:50.630
Yeah. We're actually thinking of doing something different

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.010
this year for the sake of variety.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.640
Wh-What is this?

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:02.020
Otoya, look at this!

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:08.270
You made some amazing stuff. That's great.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.070
Are you making a haunted house?

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.530
That's right. This year's bazaar is...

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.120
The Haunted House Bazaar.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.950
What? You're going to sell things in here?

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.290
The bazaar is outside!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.670
No one would come if we did that!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.830
R-Right.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.750
Hey, are you Otoya's girlfriend?

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.670
What?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.550
She's his girlfriend!

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:37.760
Otobro, way to go!

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.720
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.220
Otoya, you're blushing.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.100
Enough already!

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.650
Sheesh...

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.150
S-Sorry about that!

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.690
I-It's fine.

00:09:58.150 --> 00:10:03.660
They're all so cheerful and full of energy.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.620
Yeah. I used to get in trouble

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.460
with the principal all the time for my mischief.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:14.960
Otobro, I can't do this. Help me.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.340
Help me too.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.300
Me too.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.470
Okay, one at a time. Let me see.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.180
Oh, right.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:27.140
Nanami, sorry. I'm going to stay here a while longer.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.940
You go on ahead.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:31.940
What? No, no!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.270
Stay with us!

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:35.900
Don't go home!

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:39.610
Maybe I'll join you, then.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.570
Hooray!

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:56.710
I see.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.220
So, that's Otoya's situation.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:05.720
Otoya said he had forgotten to tell us.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:09.020
He must have been trying to be considerate.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:13.600
Just because we know doesn't mean that changes anything.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.110
Of course not.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.240
Tokiya!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.790
This is happening over our next break.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:35.290
Why don't you come?

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:37.130
A bazaar?

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.010
I noticed you've been going out a lot lately.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.760
Have you started volunteering?

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.090
No, it's...

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:47.850
It must be nice. You don't seem to have anything to worry about.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:50.430
What's wrong?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.890
It's nothing.

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:56.360
I have work that day and cannot go, but...

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:58.980
Do your best.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:00.780
Okay.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.000
We finished setting up the ghosts!

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.120
Our first customer is here!

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.500
Huh?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.380
What? What's going on?

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:21.300
Haunted houses are great for couples.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.800
Huh? Wh-What are you talking about?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.800
What?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.760
Go in!

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.390
Go, go!

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:34.520
Oh, come on. Okay, but you're next.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:38.730
Huh? Nanami?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.530
Do you not want to go with me?

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.320
I-It's not that.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:48.570
Um, haunted houses are... well...

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:49.700
You're scared!

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.000
N-No, I'm fine!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.670
Haru, you can do it!

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.010
Nanami, are you sure you're okay?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.840
I-I'm fine.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.430
It's okay. It was just a sound.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:16.520
What?

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.900
I'm sorry.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.990
Here, give me your hand.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:28.660
What?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.540
You'll be fine now.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.040
Ittoki...

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:42.000
Is it all right if we keep doing this until the exit?

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:47.550
Thank you.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:56.980
<i>Ittoki's hand is so warm and big...</i>

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:58.890
Are you okay?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:00.560
Yes.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:10.110
I think I've calmed down a little.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.990
R-Really? That's good.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.960
<i>I can't calm down at all!</i>

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.790
Shall we go, then?

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:23.630
Okay.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.190
Nanami.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.020
Huh?

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:45.440
It's okay.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:47.280
Calm down.

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:51.240
Okay.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:15:00.160
<i>Oh, man. I can't believe this is happening with Nanami.</i>

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:05.630
<i>I wish we'd never reach the exit.</i>

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.360
This is amazing.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.940
Did those children do all of this?

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:31.450
Those kids...

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:34.410
This isn't scary at all.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.580
It's so cute.

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:42.870
I'd be happy to come back to such a fun haunted house again and again.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.590
Really? I guess you're right.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:51.840
Ittoki, look at this.

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:56.800
<i>Otoya.</i>

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:58.100
<i>Haru.</i>

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.850
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:03.600
Those kids...

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:11.240
They really are your family, Ittoki.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:19.830
You're always so cheerful, kind, and warm.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:25.880
I wondered how you ended up that way.

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:36.090
I'm glad I got to come here.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:42.310
I feel like I understand you better than I did before.

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:47.310
It makes me... happy.

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:49.610
What? Really?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:58.700
I'll tell you more.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.030
I'll tell you anything, so just ask.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.910
The truth is, I...

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:11.630
I... I...

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.480
Yeah!

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.690
We did it!

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.860
It must have been the ghost I set up.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.020
Cecil, you came?

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:35.070
It sounded like fun, so here I am.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:37.860
I hope tomorrow comes soon.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:39.160
What?

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:42.740
I hope lots of customers come.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.200
I'll help out.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.170
Thanks, Cecil.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.140
We're running a bazaar!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:00.840
A bazaar!

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.010
No one's coming.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:08.350
Ittoki, there's a big flea market open

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.650
on the other side of the station today.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.520
Oh, my.

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:14.400
A flea market, huh?

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:21.370
Come on, what are you supposed to do when you feel down?

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.790
Cheer up! Let's go!

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:10.960
Go, go, Otobro!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:46.580
<i>Nanami, thank you for understanding me...</i>

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:53.710
<i>But I want you to know even more about me, Nanami.</i>

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.820
That boy's a good singer, isn't he?

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.570
Yeah, he's great.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.080
We have customers!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.490
Welcome!

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.700
This way, please!

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.700
Come on in.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:34.290
Nanami, thank you.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:36.830
Your songs are the best.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.340
No, it's the power of your singing.

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:48.180
Your singing gives everyone strength.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.350
It gives them energy.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.270
Bears!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:59.940
We finished work early, so we came to help.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.110
You mean you made us finish early.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.990
Otoya, don't be a stranger.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:07.820
Tokiya.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:13.500
I'm sorry. I actually wanted to tell you, but...

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.870
It's fine. More importantly...

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:21.130
How long are we going to stay dressed like this?

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.670
We're bears.

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:25.050
Let's play together.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.550
You must endure it for the children...

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.350
Thanks, guys.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.810
You went out of your way for me.

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:44.360
I heard the news.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:50.070
Today was a very happy day.

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:52.240
By the way, Miss Nanami...

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:58.330
Have you finished the new song for ST☆RISH I asked for?

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:00.920
Yes. I actually brought something with me today.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:03.670
I wrote a few songs.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.720
If you would choose one of them...

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:09.680
Huh?

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:14.600
